\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RanyNPformation
\item[* relevant examples:] any cheese, any books, any book
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] NPformation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) NPformationrules
\item[* date of creation:] 10-OCT-1988 12:46:12  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To introduce the BDET {\em any} syncategorematically.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\
The rule is mapped onto the same ILrule as NPformation10.
\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
The combination of {\em any} and a count singular noun exists, but it is not 
clear in which contexts it can be used as a translation of an indefinite 
article. For example:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Weet u een winkel waar ze bloemen verkopen? $\rightarrow$
Do you know any shop where they sell flowers? 
\item  Heeft ze een vraag beantwoord?
$\rightarrow$
NOT Did she answer any question? 
\end{enumerate}
Translation of {\en een} into {\em any} will often give wrong or weird results.
The reverse will not always be correct, but acceptable as a provisional
translation. Therefore the CA-pair 13  applies in analysis, but not in 
generation.

item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RNPformation12   
< m1: CN{CNrec1}[head/EN{ENrec1}]

  m2: DETP{DETPrec1}[I1:mu1] 

>

< m : I4::NP{NPrec1}[detrel/DETP{DETPrec2}[I1:mu1],
                 head/CN{CNrec1}[head/EN{ENrec1}]
                ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      < 
        I1:EXIST(mu1,[head/DET{DETrec1}[mu8]])
        I4: NPrec1 = { NPhead    : otherNP
                       person    : 3
                       class     : omegaTimeAdvclass
                       deixis    : omegadeixis
                       aspect    : omegaaspect
                       retro     : false }
        
      >

          COMP
         <
          C1: DETPrec1.superdeixis = CNrec1.superdeixis AND
              DETPrec1.posscomas * [count] <> [] AND
              DETPrec1.possnumbers * [plural] <> [] AND
              CNrec1.posscomas * [count] <> [] AND
              CNrec1.numbers = [plural]      (* EN count/plural *)
          A1: NPrec1 := 
                    {human     :yesHuman
                     animate   :yesAnimate
                     definite  :DETPrec1.definite
                     posspred  :false
                     number    :plural
                     actcomas  :[count]
                     generic   :nogeneric
                     cases     :[]
                     };
              DETPrec2 := DETPrec1;
              DETPrec2.superdeixis := omegadeixis;
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1.actcomas * [count] <> [] AND
              NPrec1 = 
                    {human     :yesHuman
                     animate   :yesAnimate
                     definite  :DETPrec2.definite
                     posspred  :false
                     number    :plural
                     generic   :nogeneric
                     cases     :[]
                     } AND
              DETPrec2.superdeixis = omegadeixis AND
              DETPrec2.posscomas * [count] <> [] AND
              DETPrec2.possnumbers * [plural] <> [] AND
              CNrec1.posscomas * [count] <> [] AND
              CNrec1.numbers = [plural]
          A1: DETPrec1 := DETPrec2;
              DETPrec1.superdeixis := CNrec1.superdeixis;
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
